        facet: "warning",
        question: "What is beriberi and what causes it?",
        answer_short: "Beriberi is the classic vitamin B1 (thiamine) deficiency disease \u2014 weakness in the limbs plus congestive heart failure. Wallach ties it to diets of polished white rice that stripped away the thiamine.",
        answer: "Beriberi is the classic thiamine (vitamin B1) deficiency disease. Wallach describes it as a common disease of the Asian rice cultures (the name is Sinhalese for 'I cannot'), characterized by weakness in the legs, hands, and arms together with congestive heart failure, with death from pulmonary edema and abdominal 'dropsy.' He identifies the cause as a thiamine (vitamin B1) deficiency \u2014 historically appearing where the diet was polished white rice with its thiamine-bearing bran removed.",
