        answer: "Two claims about the same liquid, side by side. First: it carries 77 different minerals \u2014 more than the 60 Wallach counts as essential to a human body, so a single bottle covers the full essential spectrum and then some. Second: up to 98% of what you swallow is 'bio-available,' meaning the body can actually absorb and use it rather than pass it straight through. Both, in his framing, follow from the same fact: these minerals were built by living plants, not milled out of rock. A mineral's usefulness, to him, depends on which of those two things made it.",
        verbatim: "The value of this tea colored liquid was that it\ncontained 77 minerals in the plant derived colloidal form. Because they\nwere plant derived colloidal minerals instead of from ground up rocks, they\nwere up to 98 percent bio-available.",
        page: null,
