        facet: "discovery",
        question: "How did Wallach discover colloidal minerals?",
        answer_short: "He'd never heard of them until he met the liquid being served to patients at Hospital Santa Monica, then spent three months reading everything then known about colloids.",
        answer: "How Wallach came to colloidal minerals. He had never even heard of them until he encountered the liquid being served to patients at Hospital Santa Monica. Excited by the new tool, he gathered every book and article ever written on colloids, and within three months had absorbed essentially everything then known about them.",
        verbatim: "I got excited about this new-found nutritional tool, and I gathered every\npiece of information that I could find on plant derived colloidal minerals. I\nhad never heard of colloidal minerals until this moment in my professional\ncareer so I began to educate myself. I gathered every book and every article\nthat had ever been written on colloidal minerals and within three months I\nwas familiar with just about everything historically and currently known\nabout colloids and plant derived colloidal minerals.",
        page: null,
