        facet: "stance",
        question: "Why does Wallach point to the long-lived cultures as proof?",
        answer_short: "He treats them as a living \u201Ccontrol group\u201D \u2014 five ancient peoples with disease-free longevity from steady access to all 90 essential nutrients, chiefly plant-derived colloidal minerals \u2014 and promises you can do the same.",
        answer: "Wallach's opening thesis, framed as science. He treats the world's long-lived cultures as a living 'control group' \u2014 five ancient, very different peoples who all reached healthful, disease-free longevity, with steady access to all ninety essential nutrients the body needs. The secret they shared, he says, was unique natural sources of plant-derived colloidal minerals, and his promise is that anyone who taps that same accumulated knowledge can do the same.",
        verbatim: "This control group of five\nancient and highly diverse cultures share common denominators that\ninclude healthful, disease-free longevity, and unlimited access to adequate\nlevels of all ninety essential nutrients required by humans. One of the\nsecrets they shared includes access to unique natural sources of plant\nderived colloidal minerals. My promise to you is that if you plug into the\nthousands of years of accumulated knowledge of these long-lived peoples,\nyou and yours can make it too!",
        page: null,
