        question: "What is Wallach's routine for detoxing and clearing toxic metals?",
        answer_short: "Take alfalfa daily as a detoxifier, do a monthly apple-juice liver flush, and get a yearly hair analysis to track your toxic-metal load.",
        answer: "As part of his cancer-prevention program, Wallach lays out a simple ongoing detox routine: take alfalfa daily 'in some form as a detoxifier,' do a liver flush once or twice a month by drinking apple juice for three days, and get a hair analysis each year \u2014 which he uses both to monitor toxic-metal load and to check how well you're absorbing minerals (if absorption is poor, he notes, all your mineral levels run low). It sits inside a broader daily regimen for keeping toxins down: dietary fiber at every meal, filtered (not distilled) water, 2 to 3 bowel movements a day, biodegradable household cleaners, and organic food wherever possible. The hair analysis is the feedback loop \u2014 it is how he would tell whether the metals are actually coming down.",
        verbatim: "Take alfalfa daily in some form\nas a detoxifier. Do a liver flush once or twice each month by drinking apple\njuice for three days. Do a hair analysis each year to monitor toxic metal\nload as well as absorption capability.",
        page: null,
