        answer_short: "Wallach includes zinc at 50 mg three times a day in his treatment for alopecia (hair loss).",
        answer: "In his entry on alopecia (hair loss), Wallach says hair loss occurring with eczema is often caused by an essential-fatty-acid deficiency and responds to IV interlipids and/or oral flaxseed oil (9 grams per day), and that zinc at 50 mg three times a day is also indicated. He also cites tin deficiency in male-pattern baldness. Zinc is one of his nutritional levers for alopecia.",
        verbatim: "Alopecia that occurs with eczema is\noften caused by essential fatty acid deficiency and will respond to IV\ninterlipids and/or oral flaxseed oil at the rate of 9 grams per day. Zinc at 50\nmg t.i.d. is also indicated.",
