        facet: "uses",
        question: "Is zinc oxide good for sunburn and burns?",
        answer_short: "Wallach recommends zinc oxide ointment to shield the skin \u2014 especially the nose \u2014 from sunburn, and to cover second-degree burns.",
        answer: "Wallach points to zinc oxide ointment as a topical skin protector, noting that the nose in particular may need its special protection against sunburn. For a second-degree burn with blisters, he lists covering the area with zinc oxide \u2014 or bathing it in vitamin E oil or colloidal silver \u2014 as part of care. Here zinc works from the outside as a physical barrier and skin protectant rather than as an oral supplement.",
        verbatim: "Prevention of sunburn is easy with modern \u201Csun\nscreen\u201D products. The nose may need the special protection of zinc oxide\nointment.",
