        answer_short: "Without the gelatinous bone matrix (collagen/gelatin), most supplemental calcium can't be retained in bone and is simply urinated out.",
        answer: "Wallach explains that bone matrix \u2014 the gelatinous, collagen-based foundation of bone \u2014 makes up 25 to 40 percent of total bone weight (about 40 percent in children and 25 percent in adults). Without this gelatinous matrix, most newly supplemented calcium cannot be retained in the bones, and most of what is absorbed is simply urinated out of the body. This is why his approach pairs calcium with the collagen, glucosamine, and chondroitin that form the building blocks of bone and cartilage.",
        verbatim: "Bone matrix is the gelatinous foundation of bone. Bone matrix makes up as\nmuch as 25 to 40 percent of the total bone weight, depending upon the age\nof the individual\u201440 percent in kids and 25 percent in adults. Without the\ngelatinous bone matrix, most new supplemental calcium could not be\nretained in bones and most of what is absorbed is just urinated out of the\nbody.",
