        answer_short: "At age 14, after library books tied his eyelid cramps and twitches to calcium deficiency, Wallach ate calcium-loaded calf pellets and the twitches went away in four days.",
        answer: "Wallach recounts that as a teenager troubled by cramping and twitching eyelids, he found in library health books that the cause was listed as a calcium deficiency. Knowing the calf pellets stored in his family's barn were loaded with calcium, he filled his pockets and ate them at school while classmates ate jellybeans and M&Ms. Within four days the cramps and twitches in his eyelids went away, and he realized at age fourteen that doctors knew little or nothing about nutrition.",
        verbatim: "I knew where we had calcium. The calf pellets stored in the barn were\nloaded with calcium. I ran home and filled the pockets of my shirt, jeans,\nand jacket with calf pellets. The next day in school while everyone else was\neating jellybeans and M & M\u2019s, I was, without shame, eating calf pellets. In\nfour days the cramps and twitches in my eyelids went away. I realized that\nday, at age fourteen, that doctors knew little or nothing about nutrition.",
        page: null,
