        answer_short: "GE-132, carboxyethyl germanium sesquioxide, is the organic form of germanium Asai synthesized in 1967; it is absorbed at about 30% efficiency and fully excreted within a week.",
        answer: "GE-132 is the organic germanium compound at the center of germanium's supplement story. Wallach recounts that Dr. Asai synthesized it \u2014 carboxyethyl germanium sesquioxide \u2014 in 1967 by a hydrolysis method, giving a cubic molecular structure with three negatively charged oxygen ions at its base. As an organic (chelated) form it is absorbed at about 30 percent efficiency and the entire intake clears the body within a week. He adds that ordinary food plants and animals carry only traces of germanium (beans about 4.67 ppm, tuna 2.3 ppm), while prized healing herbs \u2014 and even the famed waters of Lourdes \u2014 are unusually rich in it.",
        verbatim: "Asai synthesized GE-132, carboxyethyl germanium sesquioxide, in 1967 by\na hydrolysis method. This organic germanium structure forms a cubic\nstructure with three negative oxygen ions at the base of a cubic triangle. As\nan organic or chelate form of germanium, GE-132 is absorbed at the rate of\n30 percent efficiency and the total intake is excreted in one week.",
        page: null,
        book_id: "dddl-3e-2011",
        topics: [
          "supplements",
          "organic-germanium",
          "absorption",
          "forms"
        ]
