        verbatim: "Deficiencies of P have long been recognized in livestock. Symptoms of P\ndeficiency include the behavior of pica and cribbing and fractures.\nPhosphorus deficiency has only recently been recognized in humans. The\nwidespread, universal, and ultimately fatal results of P deficiency are the\nresult of its widespread biological functions, significantly as the result of a\ndecrease in ATP synthesis (complete metabolic energy failure) with\nassociated neuromuscular, skeletal, blood, and kidney disease.",
