        answer: "Wallach rejects the orthodox view that systemic lupus erythematosus is fundamentally an autoimmune disease in which the body attacks itself. He argues the autoimmune defect appears as a result of the disease and of abnormal proteins, rather than being its cause. Characteristically present, he says, are multiple mineral deficiencies of sulfur, copper, selenium, and others.",
        verbatim: "The \u201Corthodox\u201D theory is that\nSLE is an \u201Cautoimmune\u201D disease that causes the patient\u2019s own antibodies to\nattack themselves. The fact is the autoimmune defect occurs as a result of\nthe disease and the presence of abnormal proteins rather than being the\ncause. Multiple mineral deficiencies of sulfur, copper, selenium, etc. are\ncharacteristically present.",
