        answer_short: "For depression, Wallach's program uses dl-phenylalanine, L-tryptophan, and L-tyrosine at 2 grams three times a day each, on top of the base-line supplement program.",
        answer: "Wallach's depression protocol pairs L-tryptophan with dl-phenylalanine and L-tyrosine, each taken at 2 grams three times a day (t.i.d.). This sits on top of the base-line supplement program and steps to address food allergies and hypoglycemia, together with chromium/vanadium, B vitamins, vitamin C, calcium and magnesium, potassium, and essential fatty acids.",
        verbatim: "Treatment of depression should include dealing with the food allergies (i.e.\navoidance, rotation diets) and hypoglycemia (i.e. hypoglycemia diet). In\naddition to the base line supplement program, also use chromium/vanadium\nsupplementation at 50-200 mcg t.i.d, iron at 15 mg/day, B6, B2, Bl at 50 mg\nt.i.d., B12 at 1,000 mcg/day, vitamin C to bowel tolerance, calcium and\nmagnesium at 2,000 mg and 1,000 mg/day, potassium at 250 mg q.i.d.,\nessential fatty acids at 5 gm t.i.d., and dl-phenylalanine, l-tryptophan, and\nl-tyrosine at 2 gm t.i.d. each.",
        page: null,
        book_id: "dddl-3e-2011",
        topics: [
          "depression",
          "mood",
          "mental-health",
          "supplements",
          "protocol"
        ]
