        answer: "Shingles produces skin lesions that follow a regular pattern because the virus travels along the nerves. Wallach's treatment of choice combines the antivirals Isoprinosin at 500-1,500 mg/day and Ribavirin at 250-500 mg/day with high-dose nutrients: vitamin B12 at 1,000 mcg/day, vitamin C to bowel tolerance, vitamin E at 800-1,200 IU/day, lysine at 5 grams/day, and zinc at 15 mg three times a day.",
