        facet: "uses",
        question: "What is valine's function in the body?",
        answer_short: "In Wallach's essential-amino-acid chart, valine's function is protein production\u2014it serves as one of the raw building blocks the body uses to make its proteins.",
        answer: "In Wallach's chart of the classic essential amino acids, valine's function is listed as protein production\u2014it is one of the amino acids the body strings together as a raw building block to make its proteins. Valine shares this straightforward 'protein production' role with lysine, threonine, leucine, and isoleucine, while other essentials in the same chart play more specialized parts: tryptophan as a precursor of niacin and serotonin, phenylalanine of thyroxin and epinephrine, methionine in forming choline and creatine phosphate, and histidine in forming histamine.",
