        answer: "In Wallach's table of the essential amino acids and their functions, histidine is assigned a single job: the formation of histamine. Histamine is the signaling compound the body releases during allergic reactions and immune responses, so histidine is the raw material the body draws on to produce it. Wallach lists this same histidine-to-histamine function consistently across his books.",
