        facet: "mechanism",
        question: "Are minerals carbon-based?",
        answer_short: "No \u2014 Wallach teaches that minerals are the body's non-carbon raw materials that come from the soil, while the carbon-based nutrients (carbohydrates, fats, proteins and vitamins) are built using the sun's energy.",
        answer: "Wallach draws a fundamental line between the two kinds of raw materials the body must take in. The carbon-based nutrients \u2014 the macronutrients (carbohydrates, fats and proteins) together with micronutrients such as vitamins \u2014 are built using the energy of the sun. The non-carbon materials, chiefly the minerals, are not manufactured by living things at all; their only source is the earth's crust, the soil. Because a soil's mineral make-up varies so widely from place to place, Wallach notes that people with the same basic genetics do not all get the same opportunity for health and longevity.",
        verbatim: "The sun provides the energy to manufacture the\ncarbon-based macronutrients (carbohydrates, fats, and proteins) and\nmicronutrients like vitamins. The earth\u2019s crust\u2014the soil\u2014 is the source of\nall our non-carbon based raw materials like minerals.",
