        facet: "mechanism",
        question: "Do you need cholesterol to make testosterone?",
        answer_short: "Yes \u2014 Wallach says the body builds testosterone out of cholesterol, and warns that driving cholesterol too low can leave a man 'totally disinterested in sex.'",
        answer: "Wallach frames cholesterol as an essential raw material, not merely a villain: the body uses it to build cell walls, the myelin of the brain and spinal cord, vitamin D, bile acids, and hormones \u2014 including the adrenal-cortical hormones, estrogen, progesterone, and testosterone. Because testosterone is manufactured from cholesterol, he warns that pushing cholesterol too low backfires on men: a cholesterol deficiency, in his words, 'will turn hubby into a TV watching steer who is totally disinterested in sex.' So in Wallach's view, adequate cholesterol is a prerequisite for normal testosterone and male sex drive.",
        verbatim: "Cholesterol is an essential part\nof the structure of cell walls, brain and spinal cord (myelin), the raw\nmaterial for the production of vitamin D in the human body, bile acids,\nadrenal cortical hormones, estrogen (a cholesterol deficiency makes\nmenopause a living hell), progesterone, and testosterone (a cholesterol\ndeficiency will turn hubby into a TV watching steer who is totally\ndisinterested in sex).",
