        question: "How did Ma Lan survive the Chinese Cultural Revolution?",
        answer_short: "Arrested as an academic and sent to forced labor in the rice fields, Ma Lan kept herself alive by adding river grass and mud to her meals.",
        answer: "While in medical school during the Chinese Cultural Revolution, Ma Lan was arrested along with all academics and sent to a forced-labor program in the countryside rice fields. For three years the captives were restricted to a simple diet of corn meal, pork fat, and salt; many millions died, but Ma Lan kept herself alive by adding river grass and mud to her meals.",
        verbatim: "Ma Lan was in medical school during the Chinese Cultural Revolution. She\nwas arrested along with all academics and put in the countryside in a forced\nlabor program in the rice fields. She, along with the other captives, was\nrestricted to a simple diet of corn meal, pork fat, and salt for three years.\nMany millions died, but Ma Lan kept herself alive by adding river grass and\nmud to her meals.",
        page: null,
