        also_about: [],
        facet: "biography",
        question: "Was Ma Lan a surgeon?",
        answer_short: "As a microsurgeon Ma Lan achieved a 95 percent success rate repairing arteries and veins as thin as a human hair, versus the typical 65 percent.",
        answer: "Ma Lan was an expert microsurgeon, a skill refined over a seven-year tenure as a general surgeon at the Canton Air Force Hospital and further honed through numerous military wound repairs during the Vietnam War. Whereas most microsurgeons reported a respectable 65 percent success rate joining together the major arteries and veins, Ma Lan boasted a 95 percent success rate because of her ability to repair small arteries and veins the diameter of a human hair, in addition to repairing the larger vessels.",
        verbatim: "While most\nmicro-surgeons reported a respectable success rate of 65 percent by joining\ntogether the major arteries and veins, Ma Lan boasted a 95 percent success\nrate because of her ability to repair small arteries and veins the diameter of\nhuman hair, in addition to repairing the larger vessels.",
