        answer: `In a section titled "Homosexuality," Wallach groups homosexuality together with intersex and hermaphroditism and presents them as congenital conditions rather than emotional aberrations or a "choice of sexual preference" -- calling them "a series of preventable embryologic congenital events." He distinguishes physically normal "gay" individuals, whom he calls "less understood," from intersexuals; and in discussing the hormonal and surgical gender-assignment of intersexuals he states that a person's genetic gender (read from the Barr body, the female X chromosome, in blood smears) does not always match the brain's perception of gender because of congenital hypoplasia (underdevelopment) of the preoptic hypothalamus. He holds that such congenital events are nutritionally influenced and could be avoided with a complete preconception nutritional program.`,
