        facet: "warning",
        question: "Does fluoride in drinking water cause cancer?",
        answer_short: "Wallach accepts fluoride as an essential trace mineral (proven 1972) yet ties water fluoridation to cancer: a 1990 National Toxicology Program study found oral squamous-cell carcinoma, a rare osteosarcoma, and thyroid and liver tumors in fluoride-fed rats.",
        answer: "Wallach holds a dual stance on fluorine/fluoride. On one hand he accepts it as an essential trace mineral: prior to 1972 fluoride was thought essential only for warding off dental caries (cavities) via tooth enamel, and in 1972 the researcher Schwarz proved fluoride to be a genuine essential mineral. On the other hand he treats water fluoridation as highly controversial and links it to cancer. Following 1977 epidemiological studies by Yiamouyiannis and Burk, full-scale congressional hearings examined the charge that 10,000 excess cancer deaths were caused by fluoridating certain public water systems. The resulting U.S. National Toxicology Program animal study, reported in 1990, found increased precancerous lesions and squamous-cell carcinoma of the oral mucous membranes, a rare osteosarcoma (bone cancer) at double the rate in males as females, and a significant increase in thyroid follicular-cell tumors and liver cancer. Clinical fluoride toxicity appears as dental fluorosis at 2 to 7 parts-per-million and osteosclerosis at 8 to 20 parts-per-million, with chronic systemic toxicity at 20 to 80 milligrams per day over years; the average American already takes in about 4.4 milligrams per day from food, toothpaste, supplements and water.",
        verbatim: "In 1990 the results of the fluoride study showed an increase in rat\nprecancerous lesions in the oral mucus membrane cells; there was an increase\nin cancers of the oral mucus membranes (squamous cell carcinoma); a rare\nform of osteosarcoma appeared at double the rate in males as females;",
        page: null,
        book_id: "epigenetics",
        topics: [
          "water",
          "cancer",
          "fluoride"
        ]
