        answer: "Wallach's own one-line definition of epigenetics, and the idea behind his book's subtitle 'The Death of the Genetic Theory of Disease Transmission': most diseases that are thought to be genetically transmitted are, in fact, nutritional deficiencies that negatively impact the functions of DNA, RNA, and enzymes. His conclusion is that supplying all 90 essential nutrients lets medicine prevent and reverse most diseases, rather than writing them off as inherited fate.",
        verbatim: "epigenetics (i.e., most diseases that are thought to be genetically transmitted are\nin fact nutritional deficiencies that negatively impact the functions of DNA, RNA,\nand enzymes)",
