        answer: "Wallach points out that when cystic fibrosis was first described in 1933, it was originally thought to be the result of avitaminosis A, a vitamin A deficiency. This was because specific vitamin A deficiency changes were found in a subgroup of young patients who had been clinically diagnosed with celiac disease. He raises this history as part of his broader argument challenging the purely genetic theory of cystic fibrosis.",
        verbatim: "Initially described in 1933, CF was originally thought to be the result of\navitaminosis A (a vitamin A deficiency), because of specific vitamin A deficiency\nchanges found in a subgroup of young patients diagnosed clinically with celiac\ndisease.",
