        verbatim: "This water soluble vitamin was discovered in 1897 and isolated in 1911.\nIt is a cofactor required for energy production and optimal metabolism of\ncarbohydrates. Thiamine combines with phosphorous to form the coenzyme\nthiamine pyrophosphate (TPP), which functions as a cocarboxylase enzyme. TPP\nis required for the oxidative decarboxylation of pyruvate to form active acetate\nand acetyl coenzyme A, the critical compound of the Krebs cycle.",
