        answer: "Wallach notes that pantothenic acid deficiency looks different from one animal species to another, but common threads emerge. Animals placed on pantothenic acid-deficient diets demonstrated a reduced growth rate, anemia, nerve degenerative diseases, reduced immune functions, gastric ulcers, and a wide variety of birth defects. This animal evidence underscores how broadly the vitamin affects growth, the nervous system, immunity, and development.",
        verbatim: "The symptoms of pantothenic acid deficiency varied from one animal species\nto another. In general, however, animals that were placed on pantothenic acid-\ndeficient diets demonstrated a reduced growth rate, anemia, nerve degenerative\ndiseases, reduced immune functions, gastric ulcers, and a wide variety of birth\ndefects.",
