        facet: "basics",
        question: "What is biotin?",
        answer_short: "Biotin \u2014 also called vitamin H or coenzyme R \u2014 is a sulfur-containing B vitamin the body needs for glucose metabolism and the production of fatty acids.",
        answer: "Biotin, also known as vitamin H or coenzyme R, is a sulfur-containing B vitamin and one of Wallach's 90 essential nutrients. The body needs it for glucose metabolism and for the production of fatty acids, where it works as an essential part of enzymes that transport carboxyl units and fix carbon dioxide in animal tissue; converting it to its active coenzyme form depends on magnesium and adenosine triphosphate (ATP). A deficiency shows up in the skin and hair \u2014 eczema, baldness, and gray or white hair \u2014 which is why biotin is so closely tied to hair and skin health.",
