        question: "Can restricting methionine extend lifespan?",
        answer_short: "Wallach cites studies where restricting methionine lengthened lab-animal lifespans; a Nature fruit-fly study found that adding it back restored fertility without cancelling the lifespan gain from calorie restriction.",
        answer: "Wallach points to studies in which restricting dietary methionine increased the lifespan of laboratory animals. He highlights a study published in Nature showing that when fruit flies were kept on lifespan-extending calorie restriction, adding methionine back into their diet restored their fecundity (fertility) \u2014 yet did so without shortening the longer lifespans that calorie restriction normally produces. In effect, methionine governed fertility independently of the lifespan benefit.",
        verbatim: "Some studies have shown that restriction of methionine can increase lifespans\nof laboratory animals. A study, published in Nature, demonstrated that adding\nmethionine to the diets of fruit flies under dietary calorie restriction restored\nfecundity without reducing the longer lifespans that are typical of dietary\nrestriction.",
        page: null,
        book_id: "epigenetics",
