        answer_short: "Phenylalanine was first isolated in 1879 by Schulze and Barbieri from yellow lupine, and first synthesized in the lab in 1882 by Erlenmeyer and Lipp.",
        answer: "Phenylalanine was first reported isolated in 1879 by the scientists Schulze and Barbieri, who obtained it from the yellow lupine plant (Lupinus luteus). A few years later, in 1882, Erlenmeyer and Lipp became the first to synthesize phenylalanine artificially, building it from phenylacetaldehyde, hydrogen cyanide, and ammonia.",
        verbatim: "The first reports of the isolation of phenylalanine were made in 1879 by\nSchulze and Barbieri, who isolated the amino acid from the yellow Lupine (Lupinus\nluteus). In 1882, Erlenmeyer and Lipp first synthesized phenylalanine from\nphenylacetaldehyde, hydrogen cyanide and ammonia.",
