        answer: "Wallach lays out four types of mineral colloid, and the third is the one he describes as the most stable form found in nature. In it, carbon itself forms the protective coating around the mineral, a molecular chain roughly 10 to 12 carbon atoms long. He notes this carbon-coated colloid also occurs in bacteria, fungi, plants (including some forms of petrified wood), animals and humans. It is this carbon-coated type that he calls the most stable of the naturally occurring organic mineral colloids.",
