        answer: "After Dr. Wallach announced that cystic fibrosis was not a genetic disease but rather a congenital deficiency of the trace mineral selenium, he was summarily terminated in April 1978 from his position at Emory University's Yerkes facility \u2014 without the chance to defend his observations that a PhD candidate would have been given. The consequences followed him: also in 1978, St. Louis University hired him to be Director of its Laboratory Animal Research colony in the medical school, but after learning of his termination from the Yerkes facility by Emory University and the NIH, the university terminated him before he even moved into his new offices.",
