        answer_short: "Salt (sodium chloride) is the raw material your stomach uses to make hydrochloric acid \u2014 and that acid is what activates pepsin to digest protein, activates intrinsic factor to absorb B12, and lets you absorb minerals.",
        answer: "Chlorine (as chloride) is essential to every living species. Wallach says it powers electrochemical and catalytic functions, activates numerous enzymes, and is the basic raw material the stomach uses to make stomach acid (hydrochloric acid, HCl) \u2014 which is required to activate protein digestion by the enzyme pepsin, to absorb vitamin B12 (by activating intrinsic factor), and to absorb minerals. Ordinary salt (sodium chloride, NaCl) is the universal source of chloride ions for all living things.",
        verbatim: "Chlorine\n\n\n \n\nis essential for all living species\u2019 electrochemical and catalytic\nfunctions, activates numerous enzymes, and is the basic\nraw material for our stomachs to make stomach acid (HCl)\nrequired to activate protein digestion by the enzyme pepsin,\nB12 absorption (intrinsic factor activation), and for absorption\nof minerals.",
        page: 125,
