        answer: "To dramatize how common copper deficiency is, Wallach names famous people he says show its signs \u2014 mostly fatal aneurysms (weak arterial walls that balloon and burst, an elastin failure copper is meant to prevent): Albert Einstein (ruptured aortic aneurysm), Franklin D. Roosevelt (ruptured cerebral aneurysm), the nutritionist Paavo Airola (ruptured cerebral aneurysm), Conway Twitty and John Ritter (ruptured abdominal aortic aneurysms), and George and Barbara Bush (thyroid disease and white hair). He adds a striking autopsy statistic: 4 to 6 of every 100 Americans autopsied died of a ruptured aneurysm, and another 40% had aneurysms that had not yet ruptured.",
