        answer: "Wallach gives the body's copper content and daily needs. A well-nourished adult holds about 80\u2013120 mg of copper total, concentrated in the brain, liver, heart and kidneys; bone and muscle hold lower percentages but, by sheer mass, store about half the body's copper. Newborns carry the highest concentrations. The daily copper requirement is highest per unit of body weight in the newborn \u2014 0.08 mg per kilogram (mg/kg) \u2014 dropping to 0.04 mg/kg for toddlers and just 0.03 mg/kg for adults.",
