        answer_short: "Wallach gives fluoride's toxicity by concentration: dental fluorosis (mottled, discolored teeth) at 2-7 ppm, osteosclerosis (abnormal bone hardening) at 8-20 ppm, and chronic whole-body toxicity when daily intake stays above 20-80 ppm for several years.",
        answer: "Fluoride's toxicity thresholds \u2014 the other side of the mineral. Wallach lays out where fluoride becomes harmful by concentration: dental fluorosis (mottled, discolored teeth) appears at fluoride concentrations of 2 to 7 ppm; osteosclerosis (an abnormal hardening/thickening of bone) at 8 to 20 ppm; and chronic whole-body (systemic) toxicity when daily fluoride intake stays above 20 to 80 ppm for several years.",
