        answer: "Why carbon monoxide is so deadly \u2014 it hijacks iron's oxygen seat. Carbon monoxide, a gas produced by incomplete burning of fuel, binds to the iron in hemoglobin 200 times more tightly than oxygen does. Because it clings so hard, it crowds oxygen out of the blood \u2014 which is what makes carbon monoxide poisoning dangerous.",
