        facet: "warning",
        question: "What foods interfere with the thyroid?",
        answer_short: "Wallach names goitrogens, nitrates and nitrites in processed meats (ham, bacon, sausage, deli meats) and cruciferous vegetables (broccoli, Brussels sprouts, cabbage, cauliflower), as foods that disrupt thyroid metabolism when eaten in inordinate amounts.",
        answer: "Specific foods that disrupt the thyroid ('goitrogens'). Wallach names the foods and additives that interfere with normal thyroid metabolism and produce thyroid disease. Two groups stand out: (1) nitrates and nitrites \u2014 the preservatives in processed and cured meats: ham, bacon, sausage, bologna, salami, pastrami, pepperoni, jerky and deli meats; and (2) cruciferous vegetables \u2014 broccoli, Brussels sprouts, cabbage and cauliflower.",
        verbatim: "Many foods and food additives are known\n\n\u201Cgoitrogens\u201D because they interfere with the normal thyroid\n\nmetabolism and produce thyroid disease. These substances\n\ninclude nitrates and nitrites (i.e. ham, bacon, sausage, bologna,\nsalami, pastrami, pepperoni, jerky, deli-meats, etc.) and\ncruciferous vegetables (i.e. broccoli, Brussel sprouts, cabbage,\ncauliflower, etc.).",
