        answer: "Wallach teaches that pica is fundamentally a mineral-deficiency behavior. He describes it as a seeking or craving \u2014 with licking, chewing, and the eating of bizarre non-food substances \u2014 that has its genesis in mineral deficiencies, and he is emphatic that neither vitamin, protein, nor calorie deficiency triggers it, and that eating sugar, carbohydrate, fat, or protein will not quench it. The body is hunting for the minerals it lacks. In his survey of regional mineral-deficiency diseases, Wallach attributes the phosphate (phosphorus) deficiency form of pica specifically to South Africa.",
