        answer_short: "Scientists at the National Institute on Aging - a division of the NIH in Baltimore - working with Tufts University in Boston.",
        answer: "The ORAC test is a government-developed metric, not a supplement-industry one. It was created by scientists at the National Institute on Aging, a division of the NIH in Baltimore, working with Tufts University in Boston. The USDA went on to publish ORAC values for 277 commonly eaten foods in 2007 and a full database in 2008.",
