        answer: "Wallach's daily target is 20,000 to 25,000 ORAC points, which he gives as the optimal intake for reaching the age of 100. It is a maintenance figure, not a cure, and he never presents it alone: in the same book he pairs it with cutting free-radical foods such as fried food, trans fats, burnt fat, nitrites, alcohol and sugar, taking every essential nutrient with a special focus on minerals, and a calorie-restricted diet. He is also explicit that antioxidants by themselves raise a population's average lifespan but not its maximum.",
        verbatim: "A universally agreed upon method of predicting the antioxidant power and free radical\nneutralizing value of foods, drink and supplements is the Oxygen Radical Absorbance\nCapacity or ORAC value - based on current studies, we believe that the optimal total\ndaily intake of ORAC points to reach the age of 100 years is 20,000 to 25,000 per day.",
        page: null,
        book_id: "immortality",
        topics: [
          "orac",
          "daily-target",
          "longevity"
        ]
