        question: "How do you pick a good chocolate?",
        answer_short: "Four ways: the percentage of chocolate, the country of origin, the ORAC value, and taste.",
        answer: "Wallach gives four ways to judge a chocolate: the percentage of chocolate in the product, the country of origin, the ORAC value, and taste. He treats dark chocolate as a genuine antioxidant food on two lines of evidence. The Kuna studies found high cocoa consumption tracked with better cardiovascular health, that urban Kuna eating less cocoa lost the advantage, and that risk factors fell again when consumption rose. And in the Engler trial, 21 people ate either high- or low-flavanoid dark chocolate daily for two weeks, with the high-flavanoid group showing significantly better function in the endothelial lining of their blood vessels.",
        verbatim: "There are many ways to evaluate chocolate; one is by the\npercentage of chocolate in the product; the country of origin;\nanother is by the ORAC value; and yet another is by taste.",
        page: null,
        book_id: "immortality",
        topics: [
          "orac",
          "chocolate",
          "cocoa",
          "flavanols"
        ]
