        answer_short: "Wallach says a high-protein, low-carb diet is relatively forgiving of low vitamins but unforgiving of a low-mineral diet.",
        answer: "This is Wallach's sharpest line on why minerals outrank vitamins, and it is the third longevity piece. Mineral-rich diets are found universally across every Blue Zone and he calls them an absolute requirement to reach the centenarian club - in every case those populations have multiple sources rich in a wide spectrum of minerals. His rule of thumb: a high protein, low carbohydrate diet is relatively forgiving of a low vitamin intake, but unforgiving of a low mineral diet. Antioxidants raise your average; this is the piece that gets you to the ceiling.",
