        answer: "The fourth longevity piece is subtractive - the things that will stop you reaching 100 no matter what else you do right. Wallach's land mines are smoking, drinking excess alcohol, using street or prescription drugs, not getting second medical opinions, eating fried foods (trans fatty acids), eating burnt or well-done meats (heterocyclic amines), consuming sugar and large quantities of super-heated carbohydrates (acrylamides), and indulging in high-risk behaviour. He notes an unintended advantage of the Blue Zones: they are remote enough to have little or no access to doctors, pharmaceuticals, commercial fried food, high fructose corn syrup, soft drinks or white flour.",
