        question: "How many more years can I actually add?",
        answer_short: "Wallach calculates 25 to 50 additional HEALTHFUL years for a 150-175 lb person - and says it saves money, because cheaper food offsets the supplements.",
        answer: "Wallach puts a number on the payoff and ties it straight to cost. He calculates that a 150 to 175 pound person can add 25 to 50 additional HEALTHFUL years to their life - not years of decline - by practicing a calorie-restricted diet and faithfully following a supplement program. And it saves money rather than costing it: the reduced cost of food more than compensates for the cost of the supplements. It is the same prevent-don't-cure logic that runs through his work, and the direct rebuttal to 'I don't want to live to 150' - the years he is offering are healthful ones, and the bill is lower, not higher.",
        verbatim: "We calculate that a 150 - 175 pound person can add\n25 to 50 additional healthful years to their life with a net\nsavings in their cost of living by practicing a CR diet and by\nfaithfully employing a modified supplement program",
