        facet: "big_question",
        question: "How long can a person actually live?",
        answer_short: `Wallach: "who is to say we can't live to be 150, 175 or 200 - we believe we can!" He lists the four-minute mile and the moon landing as things the experts also called impossible.`,
        answer: "This is Wallach's boldest statement of the ceiling. He lines up a history of things the experts swore were impossible - that our hearts would explode if we drove cars at 50 mph, that no one could break the four-minute mile (then 300 runners did within a year), that the sound barrier could not be broken, that a man would never reach the moon and return - and then asks: who is to say we can't live to be 150, 175 or 200? We believe we can. It is the direct answer to the ceiling question: antioxidants raise your average, the full program raises the maximum, and Wallach puts that maximum far past 100.",
        verbatim: "it was believed that we would never\nget a man to land on the moon and return to earth and so on - who is to say we can\u2019t live\nto be 150, 175 or 200 - we believe we can!",
        page: null,
