        answer_short: "Both are everyday magnesium remedies: milk of magnesia is magnesium hydroxide used as an OTC laxative, and Epsom salts are magnesium sulfate used as a wound disinfectant and to ease the swelling of bruises, strains and sprains.",
        answer: "Wallach points to two familiar over-the-counter products built on magnesium. Milk of magnesia is a suspension of magnesium hydroxide in water, used as an everyday laxative. Epsom salts are a hydrated form of magnesium sulfate \u2014 first found in the well water of Epsom, England in the mid-1600s \u2014 and are still used today as a wound disinfectant and to reduce the swelling and inflammation of bruises, strains and sprains.",
