        answer: "Wallach explains that magnesium \u2014 a white, silvery, very lightweight metal \u2014 takes its name from its ore, magnesite (dolomite), which is primarily magnesium carbonate. That ore is believed to have first been mined in Magnesia, a district in ancient Greece. The element itself was later identified as a separate element by the British chemist Sir Humphry Davy in 1808, who used electrolysis to extract it from magnesium oxide.",
        verbatim: "Magnesium is a white silvery metal that is very light\nweight, its name is derived from the ore magnesite (dolomite)\nwhich is primarily magnesium carbonate. Magnesite is\nbelieved to have been originally mined in Magnesia, a district\nin ancient Greece.",
