        answer: "Investigators noticed that animals kept longer on fat-free diets developed inflammation and infections of the eyes \u2014 problems that were quickly reversed when fats from butter or cod liver oil were added to the diet. In 1924 the Danish investigator Bloch showed that xerophthalmia (dry, damaged eyes) in children was the same disease described in laboratory rats in 1913, and that it could be prevented or cured by adding liver, butter, or cod liver oil to the diet.",
