        answer_short: "Pyridoxine (vitamin B6) was identified in 1938 as a distinct part of the B-complex, and is really a family of three related compounds.",
        answer: "Wallach recounts that pyridoxine, or vitamin B6, was identified in 1938 as a separate entity within the vitamin 'B-complex.' Rather than a single molecule, B6 is a functional complex of three closely related chemical compounds: pyridoxine, pyridoxamine, and pyridoxal. Together these forms carry out the vitamin's roles in the body.",
        verbatim: "Pyridoxine or vitamin B, was identified in 1938 as a\nfraction or separate entity of the vitamin \u201CB-complex.\u201D Vitamin\nB, is a functional complex of three closely related chemical\ncompounds - pyridoxine, pyridoxamine and pyridoxal.",
