        answer: "In pernicious anemia, which is a B12 deficiency, taking folic acid will produce a marked improvement in the anemia itself. However, the gastrointestinal symptoms and the neurologic lesions continue to progress unchecked. Wallach calls this the 'masking effect' of folic acid, because the visible improvement in the blood hides the ongoing nerve and gastrointestinal damage of untreated B12 deficiency.",
        verbatim: "In pernicious anemia (B,, deficiency), folic acid will\nproduce a marked improvement in the anemia, however,\nthe gastrointestinal symptoms and neurologic lesions will\ncontinue to progress - this is referred to as the \u201Cmasking\neffect\u201D of folic acid.",
