        answer: "Wallach describes where chromium occurs in nature, from about 100 ppm in igneous rocks and 90 ppm in shale down to trace levels in fresh and sea water, with soils ranging from 5 to 3,000 ppm (highest in soils derived from basalt and serpentine). In living tissue, he notes, chromium accumulates in RNA and insulin.",
