        answer_short: "Sir Humphrey Davy first isolated elemental potassium in 1807 using electrolysis.",
        answer: "Potassium was first isolated in 1807 by the English chemist Sir Humphry Davy, Wallach records, who pried the highly reactive metal from its compounds using electrolysis \u2014 passing an electric current through them. He adds context that makes the element feel less abstract: the human body holds roughly 140 grams of potassium, and because a small fraction is the naturally radioactive isotope potassium-40, each of us carries a lifelong trace of internal background radiation.",
        verbatim: "Potassium was first isolated by Sir Humphrey Davy\nin 1807 using electrolysis as a means of separating elemental\npotassium from its compounds.",
        page: null,
        book_id: "immortality",
