        answer: 'Wallach explains that myoinositol \u2014 nicknamed "muscle sugar" \u2014 has a chemical structure resembling glucose and is concentrated in the brain, cerebrospinal fluid, skeletal muscle, heart muscle and other tissues. Free inositol reaches especially high levels in the organs of the male reproductive tract, particularly in semen.',
        verbatim: "Myoinositol, \u201Cmuscle sugar,\u201D has a chemical structure\nthat resembles glucose and is concentrated in the brain,\ncerebrospinal fluid, skeletal muscle, heart muscle and other\ntissues. Free inositol is found in especially high levels in the\norgans of the male reproductive tract, particularly in semen.",
