        verbatim: "Vanadium makes up 0.02% of the earth\u2019s crust, and is\npresent in trace amounts in more than 60 different ores. The\npredominant source of vanadium is vanadinite. A Mexican\nprofessor of mineralogy, Andres Manuel del Rio, discovered\nvanadium in 1801. It was later named for the Scandinavian\ngoddess Vanadis because of its many beautifully colored\ncompounds.",
