        answer: "Even though the total body content of manganese in humans is only 10 to 20 mg, it is essential to all living organisms. It activates numerous enzyme systems, including those involved in glucose metabolism, energy production, and the antioxidant enzyme superoxide dismutase (SOD). Manganese is also a major constituent of several metalloenzymes, hormones, and proteins essential to all vertebrates and humans.",
        verbatim: "The total body content of manganese in humans\nis only 10 to 20 mg. Manganese is known to be essential\nfor all living organisms. Manganese activates numerous\nenzyme systems including those involved with glucose\nmetabolism, energy production and antioxidant properties\nof superoxide dismutase (SOD). It is a major constituent of\nseveral metalloenzymes, hormones, and proteins essential to\nall vertebrates and humans.",
