        answer: "Lithium is an alkali metal so light it can actually float on water, and in Wallach's framework it is one of the essential trace minerals the body must have \u2014 not merely a psychiatric drug. He treats it as a nutrient central to mental and emotional health: he holds that depression, manic-depression (bipolar disorder), hyperactivity, ADD/ADHD, certain forms of autism, and even rage and violent behavior are, at root, hallmarks of a lithium deficiency aggravated by high sugar and alcohol intake. He points to conventional medicine's own use of lithium for bipolar disorder, and to research linking higher lithium in drinking water to lower rates of crime and suicide, as evidence of how essential this mineral is \u2014 and calls for lithium, not fluoride, to be added to public water.",
