        question: "What is faith healing (laying-on-of-hands)?",
        answer_short: "Using a person to mediate healing through belief - recorded in ancient China and Egypt and in Christianity today. Wallach notes 20-60% of patients improve on placebo when positive thought is induced.",
        answer: "Wallach describes laying-on-of-hands (spiritual and faith healers) as the use of a human being to mediate healing. 'Healers' were recorded in ancient China and Egypt, and appear in various forms today in Christianity. A spiritual healer works on the premise that whatever one believes can be made to happen by belief in God. Wallach notes that 'positive thinking' is practiced by Christians and alternative physicians alike \u2014 Robert Schuller considered positive thinking to be a form of prayer \u2014 and that twenty to sixty percent of patients will recover with placebos if positive thought is induced.",
