        answer_short: "Wallach says laetrile releases small amounts of cyanide that normal cells can detoxify but cancer cells cannot, so the cyanide selectively kills the cancer cell; it can be used as a preventive or a therapy.",
        answer: "Laetrile (amygdalin) works, in Wallach's short explanation, by releasing small amounts of cyanide: normal cells can detoxify that trace of cyanide, but cancer cells cannot, so the cyanide selectively kills the cancer cell while sparing healthy tissue. He says it can be used either as a preventive or as an active therapy, and lists it among the targeted, low-toxicity agents in his cancer survey.",
        verbatim: "LAETRILE: in short, releases small amounts of\ncyanide which normal cells can detoxify but\ncancer cells can't. The cyanide from the laetrile\nthen kills the cancer cell. Laetrile may be taken\nas a preventative measure or a therapy.",
