        answer: "Candidiasis is an overgrowth of the yeast Candida albicans \u2014 normally a harmless resident of the intestine \u2014 that turns parasitic when long-term antibiotics kill the competing gut bacteria, eventually spilling into the bloodstream. Wallach's treatment addresses food allergies, low blood sugar, and any concurrent infection, then attacks the yeast directly: oral hydrogen peroxide (1 ounce twice daily, mixed with aloe vera to make it palatable) and intravenous hydrogen peroxide in a dimethyl sulfoxide (DMSO) and 5% dextrose solution to kill the systemic infestation, with germanium taken orally and by intramuscular injection to drive oxygen into the cells (Candida dislikes oxygen). Re-seeding the gut with Lactobacillus acidophilus and autoimmune urine and blood therapies round out the program.",
