        question: "How long does it take to heal your gut?",
        answer_short: "60 to 90 days. That is how long Wallach tells dermatitis patients to expect before the intestinal lesions heal to the point where they can absorb nutrients efficiently \u2014 on a gluten-free, cow\u2019s-milk-free diet with digestive aids.",
        answer: "Dermatitis (atopic dermatitis, eczema, and dermatitis herpetiformis) is a common skin disease that Wallach says is treated incorrectly with cortisone or prednisone creams; 97% of these patients have wheat-gluten food allergies and almost as many are sensitive to cow's milk, with the same lesions occurring in the small-intestine lining and causing serious, life-threatening, immune-depleting malabsorption (a precursor to diabetes, cancer, arthritis, and birth defects). His treatment for all three forms is a gluten-free and cow's-milk-free diet, a pulse test on frequently eaten foods, essential fatty acids at 5 gm four times daily, para-aminobenzoic acid (PABA) at 200 mg four times daily, betaine HCl and digestive enzymes at 75-200 mg each three times daily before meals, vitamin A at 300,000 IU per day as beta carotene, zinc at 50 mg three times daily, and colloidal minerals on top of the base-line supplement program; healing the intestinal lesions takes 60-90 days.",
