        facet: "protocol",
        question: "How do you treat diabetes naturally?",
        answer_short: "Wallach says diabetes is easy to prevent and treat, using chromium and vanadium (vanadium able to replace insulin in adult-onset diabetes) plus zinc, B-complex, B-12, essential fatty acids, bioflavonoids, copper, lecithin, and glutathione on a high-fiber, no-processed-carb diet.",
        answer: "Diabetes, Wallach says, is easy to prevent, cure, and treat (avoiding blindness, hypertension, amputations, early death) \u2014 and since 1958 supplemental chromium has been known to prevent and treat both diabetes and hypoglycemia, with vanadium able to replace insulin for adult-onset diabetics. Diagnosis is easy: a six-hour glucose tolerance test shows blood glucose rising steeply (over 275 mg/dL at 30-60 minutes, possibly over 350 and staying elevated) with positive urine sugar. His treatment is chromium and vanadium at 25 mcg per day initially to prevent insulin shock, titrating up to 25 mcg twice then three times daily, then 50 mcg twice daily as insulin is reduced; betaine HCl and digestive enzymes at 75-200 mg three times daily before meals for the celiac-type intestinal lesions from food allergies (wheat gluten, cow's milk, soya); zinc at 50 mg three times daily; B-complex at 50 mg three times daily (including niacin, part of the glucose tolerance factor); essential fatty acids at 5 gm three times daily; vitamin B-12 at 1,000 mcg per day; bioflavonoids including quercetin at 150 mg per day; copper at 2-3 mg per day; lecithin at 2,500 mg three times daily; and glutathione at 100 mg per day, on a high-fiber diet with no processed carbohydrates. Useful herbs include licorice (Glycyrrhiza glabra), jaborandi (Pilocarpus jaborandi), yarrow (Achillea millefolium), horseweed (Erigeron canadensis), and Jerusalem artichoke.",
        verbatim: 'Treatment of diabetes should also include\nzinc at 50 mg t.i.d., B-complex at 50 mg t.i.d.\n(be sure to include niacin which is part of the\nGTF "glucose tolerance factor"), essential fatty\nacids at 5 gm t.i.d., B-12 at 1,000 mcg/day,\nbioflavonoids including quercetin at 150 mg/\nday, copper at 2-3 mg/day, lecithin at 2,500 mg\nt.i.d. and glutathione at 100 mg/day.',
