        answer_short: "Wallach recommends essential fatty acids, selenium, and vitamin E while avoiding excess vitamin D to prevent heart disease, and after a heart attack adds EDTA chelation, higher selenium and vitamin E, alfalfa, and digestive enzymes.",
        answer: "For heart disease (heart attack, cardiovascular disease) Wallach cross-references cardiovascular disease and arteriosclerosis and stresses prevention: the baseline nutritional supplements, special attention to essential fatty acids (flaxseed and/or salmon oil) while avoiding other polyunsaturated fats, selenium at 500 micrograms a day and vitamin E at 800-1,200 international units a day, moderate exercise, and avoiding vitamin D as an adult (more than 400 international units a day calcifies the coronary arteries). He urges emergency preparedness \u2014 a home oxygen tank, learning CPR, and keeping nitroglycerin and an intravenous lactated-ringers set on hand. Treatment once you have had a heart attack includes EDTA chelation (with hydrogen peroxide added) \u2014 as many as two chelations a day for 80 or more \u2014 increasing selenium to 1,000 micrograms a day and vitamin E to 1,200-2,000 international units a day, 5-10 alfalfa tablets (Alfachlor) with each meal, two ounces of Oxy-Toddy morning and night, and betaine hydrochloride and pancreatic enzymes at 75-200 milligrams three times a day before meals.",
        verbatim: 'Treatment once you have had a heart attack\nincludes EDTA chelation (with H202 added);\nyou may need as many as two chelations per\nday for 80 or more to ensure full recoveiy for\nyour heart, be aggressive - your "orthodox"\ncardiologist will not agree to this so you will\nhave to arrange it yourself!!! Increase your\nselenium intake to 1,000 mcg/day and your\nvitamin E to 1,200 to 2,000 IU/day, take 5-10\nalfalfa tablets (Alfachlor) with each meal in\naddition to the base line nutrition program.\nTake two ounces of Oxy-Toddy in the morning when you awake and two ounces before\nretiring, take betaine HCl and pancreatic enzymes at 75-200 mg t.i.d. before meals',
