        answer: "Hiccoughs are distracting and bothersome but rarely fatal \u2014 the result of spasmodic contractions of the diaphragm followed by a sudden closure of the glottis, sometimes started by swallowing hot or irritating substances. Wallach's treatment includes holding your breath (high blood carbon dioxide inhibits hiccoughs), drinking a large glass of water or orange or lemon juice slowly, applying pressure on the closed eyes with the heels of your hands, and applying digital pressure to the phrenic nerves just behind the sternoclavicular joint (where the collarbone joins the sternum).",
