        question: "How do you lower high blood pressure naturally?",
        answer_short: "Wallach stresses calcium-deficient diets as a major cause of hypertension and treats it with calcium (plant-derived colloidal minerals), a high-fiber low-fat vegetarian-leaning rotation diet, avoiding sugar/caffeine/excess vitamin D, EDTA chelation, flaxseed oil, garlic, CoQ10, lecithin, and herbs (hawthorn, rauwolfia, olive), noting weight loss can drop blood pressure dramatically.",
        answer: "Hypertension (high blood pressure) is blood pressure above 140/90 millimeters of mercury and can stem from many causes including nervousness, arteriosclerosis, kidney disease, endocrine disorders, and food allergies \u2014 and Wallach stresses that calcium-deficient diets are a major cause. Work-up includes a pulse test for offending foods and a hair analysis for heavy metals (lead, arsenic, cadmium, mercury). Treatment: calcium (especially plant-derived colloidal minerals, which are 98% absorbable) plus the baseline supplements; a high-fiber, rotation/avoidance, low-fat, vegetarian-leaning diet; avoid sugar and refined flour, caffeine, and more than 400 international units of vitamin D; autoimmune urine therapy; EDTA chelation and hydrogen-peroxide infusions; flaxseed oil at 5 grams three times daily; garlic; reduce red meat; 4-6 cups of vegetables and eight glasses of water daily; coenzyme Q10 at 60 milligrams per day; lecithin at 2,500 milligrams three times daily; and herbs hawthorn (Crataegus oxyacantha), rauwolfia (Rauwolfia serpentina), and olive (Olea europaea). Weight loss can drop elevated blood pressure dramatically.",
        verbatim: "Treatment of hypertension includes calcium\n(particularly useful is the plant derived colloidal minerals which are 98 % absorbable), high\nfiber diets, rotation/avoidance diets, autoim-\n132\nmune urine therapy, leaning toward vegetar-\nian diet, low fat diet, avoid sugar and refined\nflour, avoid more than 400 IU of vitamin D,\navoid caffeinated coffee or tea, chelation with\nEDTA.infusions with hydrogen peroxide, flax-\nseed oil at 5 gm t.i.d., garlic, reduce red meat\nintake, consume 4-6 cups of vegetables per\nday, CO-Q 10 at 60 mg/day, eight glasses of\nwater per day, lecithin at 2,500 mg t.i.d., herbs\nincluding European hawthorn (Cra-taegus\noxyacantha), rauwolfia (Rauwolfia\nserpentina), olive (Olea europaea).",
