        answer: "Itching (pruritus) can be caused by dry skin, contact with irritants, and contact or food allergies; pulse and challenge tests identify the allergens and irritants, and resolving the basic problem is essential. Symptomatic treatment: topical Caladryl, aloe vera (Aloe species), salt rubs, dilute vinegar (50%), and herbal-compress washes (see dermatitis). Oral treatment: flaxseed oil at 5 grams three times daily; zinc at 50 milligrams three times daily; vitamin A at 300,000 international units per day as beta carotene; plus the baseline nutritional program.",
