        answer: "Lentigo-maligna melanoma (a skin cancer) originates from Hutchinson's freckle on sun-exposed areas (face, neck, anus, torso) \u2014 large flat tan or brown lesions with darker spots, slow-growing (about ten years to invade the deep skin layers). Treatment can include excision biopsy or complete surgical removal; for facial tumors a cream such as Carcelim (requiring 30 days of application) may be preferable. Wallach also recommends vitamin C to bowel tolerance, vitamin A at 300,000 international units per day as beta carotene, selenium at 1,000 micrograms per day, and a #40 sunscreen to prevent new cancers, plus the baseline nutritional program.",
