        answer_short: "For liver disease and cirrhosis Wallach uses chelation with complete IV supplementation, vitamin C to bowel tolerance, vitamin A as beta carotene, B-complex, selenium, vitamin B-12, folic acid, essential fatty acids and herbs (milk thistle, parsley, tamarac, hemp agrimony), diagnosing it by elevated liver enzymes, jaundice, and other signs.",
        answer: "For liver disease (cirrhosis and nonviral hepatitis), Wallach says it is diagnosed by blood tests showing elevated liver-function markers (the SGOT, SGPT and GGT enzymes, alkaline phosphatase and bilirubin), with elevated urine ketones, jaundice, delayed clotting, a swollen tender liver under the right ribs, dry itchy skin (an essential-fatty-acid problem), anemia (iron-storage and vitamin B-12/folic-acid deficiency), weight loss and ketosis (he adds: also see gallbladder disease). His treatment is chelation with complete intravenous supplementation including amino acids and interlipids; vitamin C to bowel tolerance; vitamin A at 300,000 international units per day as beta carotene; B-complex at 100 milligrams each three times a day; selenium at 500-1,000 micrograms per day; vitamin B-12 at 1,000 micrograms per day; folic acid at 15-25 milligrams per day; essential fatty acids (both salmon oil and flaxseed oil) at 1 gram three times a day; and herbs including tamarac (Larix americana), parsley (Carum petroselinum), hemp agrimony (Eupatorium cannabinum) and milk thistle (Silybum marianum) \u2014 plus the baseline nutrition program and colloidal minerals.",
