        answer_short: "Wallach attributes meningocele \u2014 severe birth defects like spina bifida and anencephaly \u2014 to a deficiency of folic acid, vitamin B-12, or zinc and vitamin A during early pregnancy, so correcting those deficiencies before and during pregnancy is the way to prevent them.",
        answer: "Meningocele (severe anencephaly or spina bifida) is a severe birth defect in which the brain or spinal cord and its coverings (meninges) are exposed because the vertebrae form improperly. Wallach attributes it to a deficiency of folic acid, vitamin B-12, or zinc and vitamin A during early pregnancy \u2014 deficiencies that may stem from a poor diet and/or malabsorption in the mother. Severe cases may be debilitating or fatal. Treatment is limited to surgery, so he emphasizes that prevention \u2014 correcting these deficiencies before and during early pregnancy \u2014 is the goal.",
        verbatim: "MENINGOCELE (severe anencephlia or\nspina bifida): is a severe birth defect that\nresults in exposure of the brain or spinal cord\nand its coverings (meninges) because of improper formation of the vertebrae. This birth\ndefect is caused by a deficiency of folic acid, B-\n12, or zinc and vitamin A during early pregnancy",
