        answer: "Omphalocele (umbilical hernia) is a birth defect \u2014 a grape- to basketball-sized, peritoneum-lined skin sac at the navel that may contain fat and/or loops of intestine that can be pushed back into the abdomen. Wallach says it is a common birth defect caused by maternal (and therefore fetal) deficiencies of vitamin A and/or zinc. Treatment: surgery is needed if the hernial ring (the defect in the belly wall) is larger than a fingertip; if it is about a fingertip's diameter it can be healed at home without surgery by taping a golf-ball-sized ball of virgin wool firmly over the hernia and, three times a day, removing it, pushing the fat back in with the fingertip and rubbing the ring in a rotary motion for several minutes to irritate it \u2014 over weeks to months the defect fills in and heals.",
