        answer_short: "Wallach treats organic brain syndrome \u2014 his umbrella for disorders like depression, schizophrenia, dementia, and hyperactivity \u2014 by correcting nutritional deficiencies and toxicities with betaine HCl and pancreatic enzymes, niacin, essential fatty acids, chromium, and zinc plus the baseline supplement program, after a pulse test and a six-hour glucose tolerance test.",
        answer: "Organic brain syndrome is Wallach's umbrella term for a group of nutritionally-driven mental and behavioral disorders \u2014 pellagra, alcoholism, dementia, depression, hyperkinesis (hyperactivity), hypoglycemia, diabetes, premenstrual syndrome (PMS), paranoia, schizophrenia, and learning disabilities. He says they are caused by a wide variety of nutritional deficiencies (niacin/vitamin B-3, vitamin B-1, vitamin B-12, folic acid, chromium and others) and toxicities (alcohol, lead poisoning, and mercury poisoning from dental amalgam fillings). Work-up: do a pulse test to see whether food allergies are involved, and a six-hour glucose tolerance test to rule diabetes or hypoglycemia in or out (a single fasting blood-glucose reading misses 99.9 percent of hypoglycemia and 85 percent of diabetes). Treatment takes serious dedication to find and correct the underlying problems, and should include avoiding food allergens, rotation diets, betaine hydrochloride and pancreatic enzymes at 75-200 milligrams three times a day fifteen minutes before meals, niacin (vitamin B-3) at 450 milligrams three times a day as time-release tablets, essential fatty acids as salmon and flaxseed oils three times a day, chromium at 25-200 micrograms three times a day, zinc at 50 milligrams three times a day, plus the baseline nutritional supplement program.",
