        answer_short: "Wallach treats ornithosis (parrot fever) with the antibiotic tetracycline by mouth at 250-500 mg four times a day for 10-14 days, controlling the cough with codeine and enforcing strict bed rest.",
        answer: "Ornithosis (parrot fever) is an infectious disease caused by the bacterium Chlamydia psittaci. It is caught by inhaling contaminated dust from the feathers, cage bedding, or droppings of infected birds \u2014 parrots, parakeets, lovebirds, canaries, and pigeons \u2014 and produces an 'atypical pneumonia.' Symptoms include fever, chills, weakness, loss of appetite, and a dry cough that becomes productive; early on it can be mistaken for flu, Legionnaires' disease, or Q fever, so exposure to birds (especially sick ones) is the key diagnostic clue, confirmed by a blood test. Treatment is the antibiotic tetracycline by mouth at 250-500 milligrams four times a day for 10-14 days, with the cough controlled by codeine and strict, enforced bed rest \u2014 untreated, parrot fever can be fatal.",
