        answer: "Parasites (worms) include roundworms (ascaris, hookworms, pinworms, whipworms), tapeworms, and microscopic single-celled organisms (amoeba, flagellates). Symptoms include diarrhea, abdominal pain, weight loss, anal itching, weakness, and \u2014 with tapeworm \u2014 vitamin B-12 deficiency. Diagnosis is by a microscopic fecal exam for most intestinal parasites, except pinworms, which need a scotch-tape test. Treatment includes garlic (Allium sativum), peach (Prunus persica), and walnut (Juglans nigra); for heavy infestations needing stronger medication, Wallach lists pyrantel pamoate (for roundworms), niclosamide (for tapeworms), and metronidazole (for protozoa).",
