        answer: "Rachitic rosary is the beading at the junction of the ribs and rib cartilage, seen exclusively in small children kept indoors without an oral source of vitamin D; it is easily felt on examination. Wallach treats it as a sign of rickets (vitamin D deficiency). Treatment should include oral vitamin D at 400-1,000 IU per day plus the baseline nutritional supplement program including calcium and magnesium; once the abnormal bony changes normalize, drop the vitamin D dose to 250-400 IU per day, and afford daily sun exposure for at least 30 minutes.",
