        answer: "Wallach lists the body's uses of protein (functions 1-3): repairing worn-out tissue (the anabolic process), building new tissue (muscle, infant and childhood and teen growth, pregnancy), and serving as an emergency source of heat and energy (though biologically more expensive than fat or carbohydrate).",
