        answer_short: "Wallach reports at least 70 metalloenzymes \u2014 including carbonic anhydrase and alkaline phosphatase \u2014 require zinc, which helps bind enzymes to their substrates and is also needed by RNA polymerase and thymidine kinase.",
        answer: "Wallach reports that no fewer than 70 metalloenzymes require zinc to function \u2014 including carbonic anhydrase, alkaline phosphatase, lactic dehydrogenase, and carboxypeptidase. Zinc helps bind enzymes to their substrates by maintaining the correct spatial and configurational relationships, and some enzymes bind zinc so tightly that they keep functioning even during severe zinc depletion. Zinc is also required by the DNA-dependent RNA polymerase and thymidine kinase.",
