        answer: "Wallach ties arthritis to a cluster of mineral deficiencies. He lists arthritis among the common calcium deficiency diseases, with magnesium, boron, copper and sulfur named as complicating-factor deficiencies. Sulfur deficiency in particular produces the degenerative types of arthritis \u2014 it lets the cartilage, ligaments and tendons degenerate (the same collapse of connective tissue he links to lupus and the other \u201Ccollagen diseases\u201D). In short, the deficiencies he blames for arthritis are calcium, magnesium, boron, copper and sulfur.",
