        answer: "Wallach warns that canned tuna carries nearly double the lead of fresh tuna. The cause he names is the sealant material used to close the seams of steel and tin cans, which leaches lead into the food \u2014 one of several dietary lead sources he catalogs (alongside leaded-gasoline residue in soils, lead paint chips and dust, and lead-glazed decorative pottery mistakenly used as food containers) contributing to the lead burden in the American food chain.",
        verbatim: "Another source of lead in our food chain\nis the sealant materials used to close the\nseams in steel or tin canned foods. One\nstudy showed that canned tuna has nearly\ndouble the level of lead as fresh tuna",
