        answer: "Wallach argues that molybdenum is among dozens of the sixty formerly abundant soil elements - alongside selenium, arsenic, tin, aluminum, chromium, vanadium, and nickel - that the allopathic medical profession, just a short time ago, considered totally toxic with no possibility of essentiality. He contends they made sure these elements were kept out of our food. This, in his view, is part of why our Earth's soils and food supply are now depleted of nutrients the body needs.",
        verbatim: "Dozens of the sixty formerly abundant soil elements (selenium, arsenic, tin, aluminum, chromium, vanadium, molybdenum, nickel, etc.) were, just a short time ago, thought to be totally toxic with no possibility of essentiality by the allopathic medical profession and they made sure they were not in our food!!!",
